&lt;h2 id="foreword"&gt;Foreword
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;My zodiac year is here~! As an algebra enthusiast (self-proclaimed, really just a terminology tourist), I&amp;rsquo;ve recently seen a lot of videos on Bilibili about how to prove the Snake Lemma, like &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1FZFNezE6D" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;this one&lt;/a&gt;. I ran into this lemma back when I was trying to teach myself algebra, but by the time I got to that part I was already about to pass out (probably right after seeing this part I dropped the book, &lt;em&gt;Algebra: Chapter 0&lt;/em&gt;), so it&amp;rsquo;s almost like I never learned it. Having seen so many videos about the Snake Lemma recently, of course I want to learn it properly, and here I&amp;rsquo;ll make a record of it. In this article you will encounter:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Multiphase Field Model and Grand Potential Equation</title><link>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/pf_note/mpf_gp/</link><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://a-moment096.github.io/en/posts/pf_note/mpf_gp/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://a-moment096.github.io/images/ShoujouRei_MikitoP.png" alt="Featured image of post Multiphase Field Model and Grand Potential Equation" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Recording the two phase field models currently in use, including their derivations, assumptions, and shortcomings&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The header image is by &lt;a class="link" href="https://twitter.com/katorei_" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
